# ─── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=5000

# ─── Supabase / PostgreSQL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get this from: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Database → Connection string (URI)
# Use the "Transaction" pooler for apps or the direct URI for migrations.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres
Step-by-step bootstrap
1. Run migrations (creates all tables + seeds the 7 roles)

cd backend
npm run migrate:supabase
2. Seed the first admin accounts

npm run seed:admin
This creates two accounts instantly:

Role	Email	Password
Super Admin	admin@school.com	Admin@1234
Registrar	registrar@school.com	Reg@1234
You can override these with env vars: SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL, SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD, SEED_REGISTRAR_EMAIL, SEED_REGISTRAR_PASSWORD

3. Start the backend

npm run dev
4. Start the frontend (separate terminal)

cd frontend
npm run dev
The full login → register → login flow
Registrar logs in at /login
  → email: registrar@school.com  password: Reg@1234
  → redirected to /registrar/dashboard

Registrar goes to Register User
  → selects Student tab
  → fills in name, DOB, address, email, password
  → clicks "Register Student"
  → sees: Student Number: STU-2026-0001, Admission: ADM-2026-0001

Student logs in at /login
  → email + password set by registrar
  → redirected to /student/dashboard immediately ✅
No email confirmation, no manual DB inserts — just registrar creates the account and the person can log in straight away.

Est. Credits Used: 1.82
Elapsed time: 1m 15s